{{smaller block|The painter who is content with the praise of the world in respect to what does not satisfy himself, is not an artist, but an ''artisan.''
{{right|''Allston.''}}
The soldier was on a sudden converted into an ''artisan'', and, instead of war, the camp echoed with the sounds of peaceful labor.
{{right|''Prescott'', Ferd. and Isa., I. 15.}}}}
'''2†.''' One skilled in a fine art; an artist.
{{smaller block|<poem>Best and happiest ''artisan'',
Best of painters.</poem>
{{right|''Guardian.''}}}}

